## What is SEO strategy consulting?

SEO strategy consulting is expert direction for a business that wants better organic search results without buying full-service implementation. My sessions cover a current state analysis, the opportunities worth taking, prioritised recommendations and the next steps. Your marketers and developers keep doing the work. I set the order and check the approach. It suits in-house teams that need specialist input and businesses deciding whether to invest in SEO at all. I am based in Reading in Berkshire and work with UK teams online.

## Why does in-house SEO stall without direction?

In-house SEO stalls when activity runs in the wrong order. Content, technical fixes and rank tracking each need a priority set against your competitors.

Typical symptoms are content that ranks briefly then disappears, technical fixes that do not move rankings and an archive of posts that earns little traffic. The usual cause is a lack of direction.

The fix is a ranked order of work.

- **Advice:** I assess priorities and guide your team; your team implements. [Book advisory](/contact/?support=ongoing_advice#contact)
- **Implementation:** I plan and deliver the agreed SEO work. [Discuss implementation](/contact/?support=ongoing_implementation#contact)
- **One session:** a single 90-minute session for one decision or problem. [Ask about a session](/contact/?support=single_session#contact)

My £495 technical SEO audit gives a full documented diagnosis before consulting begins. It covers technical, content and AI-visibility issues in 5 working days.

## SEO support for in-house marketing and development teams

**I support in-house teams in three ways: advice for marketers, training for the whole team and developer-ready fix lists for engineers. Your team keeps doing the work. I set the priorities, check the approach and answer the questions that hold the work up.**

Most in-house teams have two groups with different needs. Marketers need to know which pages and topics to work on first. Developers need precise tickets they can estimate and ship. I cover both at fixed prices.

| Team need | Format | Price |
|---|---|---|
| A second opinion on one decision or problem | Single 90-minute session with written follow-up | £200 |
| Ongoing direction for the marketing team | Monthly advisory, four hours a month | £600 per month |
| A periodic check on a programme already running | Quarterly strategy review | £500 |
| Skills for the whole team, on your own site | [SEO training](/services/seo-training/) workshop, up to 8 people | £750 half day, £1,250 full day |
| A ranked fix list developers can work through | [Technical SEO audit](/services/technical-seo-audit/) with a developer-ready spreadsheet | £495 fixed |
| Someone to carry out the work | [SEO retainer](/services/seo-retainer/) | From £1,500 per month |

I am not VAT-registered. No VAT is added to these prices. The audit spreadsheet lists the affected URLs, the issue, the recommended fix and an effort estimate for each item. Developers can turn each row into a ticket. In monthly advisory I can review those tickets before they ship and check the result afterwards.

### Should you hire in-house, use an agency or a consultant?

Hire in-house for the work that happens every week. Buy specialist work from a consultant as you need it. Use an agency when you need a volume of execution and nobody internal to manage it. Bringing SEO in-house works best when you split the work this way.

1. **Hire for daily execution.** A content-focused SEO or marketer who can brief, publish, update pages and read Search Console.
2. **Keep specialist work external.** Technical audits, migrations, algorithm-update diagnosis and strategy reviews happen a few times a year. Paying for them as needed is usually cheaper than a full-time specialist.
3. **Use consulting to bridge the gap.** Monthly advisory gives a new hire someone senior to check priorities with. Training brings the rest of the team up to speed. An audit gives developers a clear backlog from day one.

Advisory can drop to occasional single sessions once the team is confident. My guide to [in-house SEO vs agency vs consultant](/blog/inhouse-seo-vs-agency-vs-consultant/) covers the wider trade-offs.

