## What do SEO consulting sessions include?

A session covers the questions you bring. It draws on the four components below and can take in any of the topics listed after them.

### Current state analysis

A review of your existing SEO performance: organic traffic trends, keyword rankings, technical health and content quality. I read your Google Search Console data to see what is working and what is holding growth back.

### Opportunity identification

An analysis of competitor strategies, search demand in your industry and gaps in your current approach.

Opportunities might include quick-win optimisations, a [topical map](/services/topical-maps/) for authority building or technical fixes that block rankings.

### Prioritised recommendations

Recommendations ranked by effort and impact. Each one includes implementation guidance, the expected outcome and the resource it needs.

### Sequencing

The order of initiatives: which to tackle first, how they connect and what success looks like.

### Topics a session can cover

| Topic | What a session covers |
|---|---|
| Technical SEO strategy | Crawlability, indexation, site speed and mobile optimisation |
| Content strategy | [Semantic SEO methodology](/services/semantic-seo/), topical authority building and publication planning |
| Local SEO | Google Business Profile optimisation, local citation strategy and location page development |
| Keyword research | Search demand analysis, query network mapping and prioritisation frameworks |
| Internal linking | Hub-and-spoke architecture, anchor text strategy and link distribution |
| Performance analysis | Traffic pattern interpretation, ranking volatility diagnosis and algorithm update assessment |

## Who is SEO consulting for?

SEO consulting suits four business situations. Each gets something different from a session.

| Your situation | What SEO consulting gives you |
|---|---|
| In-house marketing team handling SEO | Specialist input on strategy, technical problems and algorithm changes without replacing the team |
| Business between agencies | An objective view of the current state and clear direction for the next step |
| Startup or growing business | Strong SEO foundations before scaling content, so resources go to high-impact work |
| Business evaluating SEO investment | An honest view of likely return and realistic timelines before committing budget |

