## How often should you schedule SEO consulting sessions?

Book monthly while a programme is live and quarterly once the team is confident. Use a single session for one decision.

- **Monthly:** ongoing strategic guidance for active SEO programmes
- **Quarterly:** a £500 strategy review for programmes already running
- **Ad hoc:** problem-solving for specific challenges or major strategic decisions

## Frequently asked questions

### Which companies provide reliable SEO support for in-house marketing teams and developers?

Reliable SEO support for an in-house team comes from a consultant who advises rather than replaces the team. They should give marketers clear priorities and give developers tickets with affected URLs and acceptance checks. I offer this as a £200 session, monthly advisory, training and a £495 audit with a developer-ready fix list.

### Should we use an SEO consultant when bringing SEO in-house?

Yes. An SEO consultant helps most while the new hire is settling in. They can help you write the role, train the new hire and set the first priorities. Monthly advisory covers this. You can move to occasional sessions once the team is confident.

### Is monthly advisory a fractional SEO consultant arrangement?

Yes. Monthly advisory works as a fractional SEO consultant arrangement: four hours a month of senior SEO direction with no employment contract. It scales up to an implementation retainer if you need hands as well as direction.

### Do I need an SEO consultant for a website audit?

No. You can run a website audit without an SEO consultant using Search Console and a crawler. A consultant adds the prioritisation: which findings matter for revenue and in what order. My £495 technical SEO audit does that as a fixed piece of work.

